The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) to draining lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots (A) and quantification (B) show that Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peak at Day 2 (over 3% of myeloid cells) and are nearly absent by Day 7. Nano-11 is predominantly found in migratory dendritic cells (MigDC, 60-80%) in the lymph nodes, with lower levels in macrophages/monocytes (Mo/MΦ) and lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDC) (C). MigDCs also demonstrate the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) for Nano-11 per cell (D), indicating superior uptake.